\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DZL}{\texttt{Stacks tag 0DZL}}


In Example \ref{examples-defos-example-rings} let $P$ be a smooth $k$-algebra. Then
$T\Deformationcategory_P = (0)$.

\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY4}{\texttt{Stacks tag 0DY4}}


In Lemma \ref{examples-defos-lemma-rings-TI} if $P$ is a finite type $k$-algebra, then
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\text{Inf}(\Deformationcategory_P)$ is finite dimensional if and only if
$\dim(P) = 0$, and
\item $T\Deformationcategory_P$ is finite dimensional if
$\Spec(P) \to \Spec(k)$ is smooth except at a finite number of points.
\end{enumerate}

\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY8}{\texttt{Stacks tag 0DY8}}


Example \ref{examples-defos-example-schemes}
satisfies the Rim-Schlessinger condition (RS).
In particular, $\Deformationcategory_X$ is a deformation category
for any scheme $X$ over $k$.

\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DYZ}{\texttt{Stacks tag 0DYZ}}


In Situation \ref{examples-defos-situation-glueing}
there is an equivalence
$$
\Deformationcategory_X =
\Deformationcategory_{P_1}
\times_{\Deformationcategory_{P_{12}}}
\Deformationcategory_{P_2}
$$
